  "archive_id": "BW2-B86-P08",
  "title": "Direct Scalene Triangular Facets of Convex Polyhedra Must Be Acute",
  "batch_label": "86",
  "kind": "resolution-paper",
  "original_status": "proved",
  "scope": "For every nondegenerate scalene Euclidean triangle T with side lengths 0 < a < b < c < a+b and c^2 >= a^2+b^2, and for either fixed planar orientation of T, there is no full-dimensional compact convex three-polytope all of whose facets are direct copies of T, where directness means agreement of the cyclic side-length order induced by the outward normal. Equivalently, every scalene triangle admitting such an orientation-preserving monohedral realization is acute.",
  "gate_basis": "Current released terminal, manifest, PDF, TeX freeze, snapshot files, provenance and four audits agree.",
